aign data and track site usage for the site's analytics report. The cookie stores information anonymously and assigns a randomly generated number to recognise unique visitors. Cookie _gid Duration 1 day Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store information on how visitors use a website while also creating an analytics report of the website's performance. Some of the collected data includes the number of visitors, their source, and the pages they visit anonymously. Cookie _gat_gtag_UA_* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store a unique user ID. Cookie _ga_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store and count page views. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets the cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Cookie vuid Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Vimeo installs this cookie to collect tracking information by setting a unique ID to embed videos on the website. Cookie _hjSessionUser_* Duration 1 year Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjSession_* Duration 1 hour Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjTLDTest Duration session Description To determine the most generic cookie path that has to be used instead of the page hostname, Hotjar sets the _hjTLDTest cookie to store different URL substring alternatives until it fails. Cookie _gat_UA-* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie for user behaviour tracking. Cookie _scor_uid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Stores a unique identifier to measure audience size, analyze browsing behavior, and improve advertising relevance and content performance across websites. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyse the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Cookie AWSALB Duration 7 days Description AWSALB is an application load balancer cookie set by Amazon Web Services to map the session to the target. Cookie __utma Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to distinguish users and sessions. The cookie is created when the JavaScript library executes and there are no existing __utma cookies. The cookie is updated every time data is sent to Google Analytics. Cookie __utmc Duration session Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to enable interoperability with urchin.js, an older version of Google Analytics and is used in conjunction with the __utmb cookie to determine new sessions/visits. It is deleted when the user closes the browser. Cookie __utmz Duration 6 months Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store the traffic source or campaign by which the visitor reached the site. Cookie __utmt Duration 10 minutes Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to inhibit the request rate. Cookie __utmb Duration 1 hour Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to determine new sessions/visits. __utmb cookie is created when the JavaScript library executes and there are no existing __utma cookies. It is updated every time data is sent to Google Analytics. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie IDE Duration 1 year 24 days Description Google DoubleClick IDE cookies store information about how the user uses the website to present them with relevant ads according to the user profile. Cookie test_cookie Duration 15 minutes Description doubleclick.net sets this cookie to determine if the user's browser supports cookies. Cookie elfsight_viewed_recently Duration Less than a minute Description Stores identifiers of recently viewed pages or products to display a personalized recently viewed widget and improve navigation across sessions. Cookie _hashV Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Stores a hashed visitor identifier to preserve portal preferences, attribute marketing campaigns, and optimize campus-visit scheduling, analytics, and user experience. Cookie YSC Duration session Description Youtube sets this cookie to track the views of embedded videos on Youtube pages. Cookie VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to measure bandwidth, determining whether the user gets the new or old player interface. Cookie VISITOR_PRIVACY_METADATA Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to store the user's cookie consent state for the current domain. Cookie NID Duration 6 months Description Google sets the cookie for advertising purposes; to limit the number of times the user sees an ad, to unwanted mute ads, and to measure the effectiveness of ads. Cookie __Secure-YEC Duration past Description Description is currently not available. Cookie __Secure-YNID Duration 6 months Description Suivi d'audience et de comportement de lecture du lecteur vidéo YouTube. Uncategorised Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Powered by Working at Bishop's Close Search for: Search Career Opportunities Human Resources Menu Thérapeute du sport (2 postes) / Athletic Therapists (2 positions) Staff sur le campus / on campus 28 October 2025 Closes: 27 September 2026 Université Bishop's / Bishop's University Overview Affichage 25-43 (Poste régulier à temps partiel) Les énoncés suivants sont destinés à décrire la nature et le niveau de travail général. Ils ne représentent pas une liste exhaustive de toutes les responsabilités, tâches et aptitudes requises. L’Université Bishop’s recherche un ou un·e thérapeute du sport pour un poste régulier à temps partiel. Relevant de la gestionnaire de la médecine sportive, la personne titulaire du poste fournira des services de thérapie du sport et participera à l’évaluation, à la prise en charge et au traitement des blessures sportives aiguës et chroniques des athlètes des équipes de l’Université Bishop’s. Elle concevra des programmes de réadaptation et intégrera les modalités thérapeutiques nécessaires, au besoin. Elle contribuera également à la prévention des blessures sportives à l’aide de diverses techniques de bandage prophylactique et de contention, ainsi qu’en offrant de la formation sur les bonnes pratiques d’entraînement.  La semaine de travail est de 40 heures, avec un horaire irrégulier incluant les soirs et les fins de semaine. Les deux postes ont des périodes de travail distinctes : l’un s’étend de la mi-juillet à la mi-mai et l’autre du début août à la fin mai. Nature des tâches Fournir une couverture de thérapie sportive sur place lors des entraînements, des matchs à domicile et à l’extérieur ; Appuyer la formation et la supervision des étudiant.e.s agissant à titre d’étudiante·s-formateur·trice·s, et contribuer à la présentation de séminaires éducatifs sur les commotions cérébrales et les programmes du Centre canadien pour l’éthique du sport (CCES) ; Collaborer avec les autres membres des services de médecine sportive, des services de santé et du département des sports afin d’assurer la prestation de soins de qualité aux athlètes et aux patient·e·s ; Soutenir et contribuer aux activités quotidiennes de la clinique de médecine sportive ; Appuyer la mise en œuvre et le respect des consignes sanitaires de santé publique par les étudiant·e·s; Offrir un soutien administratif pour la facturation des assurances, la prise de rendez-vous, les rapports financiers, l’évaluation et la tenue des dossiers annuels ; Faire preuve de flexibilité quant à l’horaire de travail, puisque la majorité des tâches exigent la capacité de travailler selon un horaire non traditionnel, souvent pendant de longues périodes en dehors des heures normales de travail ; Effectuer toute autre tâche assignée. Qualifications et exigences Diplôme de premier cycle en sciences de l’exercice ou dans un domaine connexe, avec spécialisation en thérapie du sport ; Être thérapeute du sport agréé·e et en règle auprès de l’Association canadienne des thérapeutes du sports (ACTS) ; Posséder un minimum de deux (2) années d’expérience dans un rôle similaire, et une bonne connaissance du travail auprès d’athlètes et d’entraîneur·e·s de haut niveau ; Capacité à travailler efficacement de façon autonome et en équipe, en faisant preuve d’initiative, en offrant un excellent service à la clientèle et en respectant le code de déontologie de l’Association canadienne des thérapeutes du sport (ACTS) ; Faire preuve de professionnalisme à l’intérieur et à l’extérieur de la clinique ; Capacité de travailler dans un environnement complexe et en constante évolution ; Excellent jugement, sens du tact et diplomatie face à une clientèle variée ; Maîtrise du français et de l’anglais, à l’oral et à l’écrit. À propos de l’Université Bishop’s Fondée en 1843, l’Université Bishop’s est située au cœur de l’arrondissement de Lennoxville, à Sherbrooke au coeur des Cantons-de-l’Est, au Québec. Elle est reconnue pour son modèle d’éducation libérale, ses classes de petite taille et son environnement résidentiel favorisant une expérience étudiante personnalisée. Situés à Sherbrooke, à environ une heure et demie de route au sud-est de Montréal, les Cantons-de-l’Est offrent une atmosphère accueillante et sécuritaire, des activités récréatives de plein air exceptionnelles et une excellente qualité de vie. L’Université Bishop’s est située sur le territoire traditionnel des Abénaquis. Nous reconnaissons leur gestion de cette terre et apprécions le fait que nous sommes tous des invité·e·s sur le territoire abénakis. Bishop’s est une université anglophone et offre principalement des programmes de 1 er cycle. Bishop’s offre plus de 100 programmes d’études au sein de cinq divisions : sciences humaines, sciences naturelles et mathématiques, sciences sociales, administration et éducation. Le campus de 550 acres comprend 25 bâtiments, dont sept résidences, deux bibliothèques, deux théâtres, des salles de classe exceptionnelles, des laboratoires et des installations sportives, un aréna, une chapelle historique, une salle de concert, une garderie ainsi qu’un étang, un refuge faunique et un terrain de golf. Ce que nous offrons à nos employé·e · s : un programme d’assurance collective qui comprend : l’assurance médicament et médicale , les soins de la vue et l’assistance-voyage; des vacances généreuses ainsi qu’un congé de 10 jours entre décembre et janvier; des horaires flexibles et la possibilité de travailler à domicile lorsque la nature du rôle le permet; des tarifs préférentiels au centre sportif et au terrain de golf; un régime de retraite à prestations déterminées et/ou régime de retraite simplifié; un programme d’aide aux employés et à la famille (PAEF); des initiatives en matière de développement durable et de bien-être; l’accès à des événements culturels et éducatifs en continu. Classification:       Classe 8     24.57 $ à 32.09 $    de  l’heure    ( poste syndiqué) L’Université Bishop’s applique un programme d’Accès à l’égalité en emploi issu de la Loi sur l’Accès à l’égalité en emplois des organismes publics. L’Université accueille les candidate · e · s qui s’engagent à respecter les valeurs d’équité, de diversité et d’inclusion et qui nous aideront à accroitre notre capacité en matière de diversité et d’inclusion.  Nous encourageons les candidatures de membres de groupes historiquement défavorisés et marginalisés, notamment les peuples autochtones, les membres des minorités visibles et ethniques, les personnes handicapées, les femmes et les personnes LGBTQ2S+. S.V.P. faire parvenir votre curriculum vitae ainsi qu’une lettre de présentation , en indiquant pour quel poste vous appliquez à careers@ubishops.ca . Le poste restera ouvert jusqu’à ce qu’il soit pourvu. Tel que prévu à la convention collective, la priorité sera accordée à un·e candidat·e interne qualifié·e. Veuillez noter que seules les personnes retenues pour une entrevue seront contactées, et que des tests de sélection peuvent être administrés ; merci pour l’intérêt manifesté. Dans le processus de recrutement, nous fournissons un soutien aux personnes handicapées afin de répondre aux besoins en prévenant et en éliminant les obstacles à l’accessibilité. Si vous nécessitez de mesures d’adaptation pour participer en tant que candidat · e dans le processus de recrutement, veuillez contacter careers@ubishops.ca ________________________________________________________________________ Posting 25-43 (R egular part-time position) The following statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed. They are not representing an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required. Bishop’s University is seeking an Athletic Therapist for a regular part-time position.  Reporting to the Manager of Sports Medicine, the incumbent will provide athletic therapy services and assist with the assessment, management, and treatment of acute and chronic athletic injuries among the varsity teams at Bishop’s University. Designing rehabilitative programs and incorporating necessary therapeutic modalities when needed, the incumbent will also assist in the prevention of athletic injuries using various prophylactic taping and bracing techniques, as well as education towards training. This position has a work week of 40  hours from Monday to Friday as well as irregular schedules including weekends and evenings. The two positions have distinct working periods: one position runs from mid-July to mid-May, while the other one from early August to end of May. Nature of duties and responsibilities Provide on-site athletic therapy coverage for practices, home and away games; Support the education and supervision of students who act as student trainers; and assist in delivering CCES and concussion education seminars; Collaborate with other members of the Sports Medicine, Health Services and Athletics departments to ensure quality health care delivery for athletes and patients; Support and assist with the Sports Medicine Clinic’s daily operations; Support and assist with ensuring students follow all public health sanitary guidelines; Offer administrative support for insurance billing, appointment scheduling, financial reports, evaluation and maintenance of annual records; Flexible schedule as most tasks require the ability to work non-traditional hours, often for extended periods of time outside the course of a typical working day; Other tasks as assigned. Qualifications and Requirements Undergraduate degree in exercise science or related field, with specialization in Athletic Therapy; Must be a Certified Athletic Therapist in good standing with the Canadian Athletic Therapy Association (CATA); Minimum of 2 years of experience in a similar role and familiarity in working with athletes and coaches at a high-performance level; Ability to work effectively both independently and in a team environment, displaying initiative, excellent customer service, and abiding by the CATA code of ethics; Maintain professionalism inside and outside the clinic; Ability to work in a complex, ever-changing environment; Excellent judgment, tact and diplomacy in dealing with a varied clientele; Excellent verbal and written communication skills in both English and French. About BU Founded in 1843, Bishop’s University is located in the Lennoxville borough of Sherbrooke, in the Eastern Townships of Quebec. It is recognized for its liberal education model, its small class sizes, and its residential environment that fosters a personalized student experience. Located about an hour and a half southeast of Montreal, the Eastern Townships offer a welcoming and safe atmosphere, exceptional outdoor recreational opportunities, and an excellent quality of life. Bishop’s University is situated on the traditional and unceded territory of the Abenaki people. We acknowledge their historical relationship with this land and are grateful to be guests on Abenaki territory. Bishop’s is an English‑language university offering primarily undergraduate programs, with more than 100 academic programs across five divisions: Humanities, Natural Sciences and Mathematics, Social Sciences, Business, and Education. The 550‑acre campus includes 25 buildings, seven residences, two libraries, two theatres, exceptional classrooms, laboratories, athletic facilities, an arena, a historic chapel, a concert hall, and a daycare centre. The campus also features a pond, a wildlife refuge, and a golf course. What We Offer – Employees benefit from: Medical, vision, health and travel insurance; Generous vacation as well as a 10-day holiday break between December and January; flexible scheduling and work from home possibility when applicable employee discounts to our sports center and Golf course; defined benefit and/or simplified pension plan; Employee Family Assistance Plan (EFAP); Sustainable development and Wellness initiatives; Access to ongoing cultural and educational events. Classification:       Class 8     $24.57 to $32.09   per hour     ( unionized position) Bishop’s University implements an equal access employment / program under the Act respecting equal access to employment in public bodies. The University welcomes applicants who are committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity and inclusion and who will assist us expand our capacity for diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from members of groups that have been historically disadvantaged and marginalized, including Indigenous peoples, visible and ethnic minorities, persons living with disabilities, women and LGBTQ2S+ persons. If interested, please submit your curriculum vitae and cover letter, including what position you are applying for to careers@ubishops.ca . This position will remain open until filled. Per the Collective Agreement, priority will be given to qualified internal applicants. Please note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted and testing may be required; thank you for your interest. We provide support in the recruitment processes to applicants with disabilities, including accommodation that takes into account an applicant’s accessibility needs. If you require accommodation in order to participate as a candidate in the recruitment process, please contact careers@ubishops.ca To apply for this job email your details to careers@ubishops.ca . Staff To apply for this job email your details to careers@ubishops.ca . Company Social Website © 2025 Bishop's University — All Rights Reserved Back to Top"
    },
    "https://jobboard.ubishops.ca/": {
      "title": "Job and Internship Board for Students",
      "description": "Job and Internship Board for Students We value your privacy We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience and analyse our traffic. By clicking \"Accept All\", you consent to our use of cookies. Cookie policy Customise Reject All Accept All Customise Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorised as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site.... Show more Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. Cookie cookiesession1 Duration 1 year Description This cookie is set by the Fortinet firewall. This cookie is used for protecting the website from abuse. Cookie __cf_bm Duration 1 hour Description This cookie, set by Cloudflare, is used to support Cloudflare Bot Management. Cookie _cfuvid Duration session Description Calendly sets this cookie to track users across sessions to optimize user experience by maintaining session consistency and providing personalized services Cookie userReferer Duration 1 month Description No description available. Cookie guest Duration 1 month Description No description available. Cookie _node Duration session Description No description available. Cookie _hash Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description No description available. Cookie AWSALBCORS Duration 7 days Description Amazon Web Services set this cookie for load balancing. Cookie rc::a Duration Never Expires Description This cookie is set by the Google recaptcha service to identify bots to protect the website against malicious spam attacks. Cookie rc::c Duration session Description This cookie is set by the Google recaptcha service to identify bots to protect the website against malicious spam attacks. Cookie ASP.NET_SessionId Duration session Description Issued by Microsoft's ASP.NET Application, this cookie stores session data during a user's website visit. Cookie AWSELB Duration session Description Associated with Amazon Web Services and created by Elastic Load Balancing, AWSELB cookie is used to manage sticky sessions across production servers. Cookie wpEmojiSettingsSupports Duration session Description WordPress sets this cookie when a user interacts with emojis on a WordPress site.  It helps determine if the user's browser can display emojis properly. Cookie ci_session Duration 2 hours Description This cookie is set as default session Cookie name in config.php in config folder in CodeIgniter. Cookie _GRECAPTCHA Duration 6 months Description Google Recaptcha service sets this cookie to identify bots to protect the website against malicious spam attacks. Cookie PHPSESSID Duration session Description This cookie is native to PHP applications. The cookie stores and identifies a user's unique session ID to manage user sessions on the website. The cookie is a session cookie and will be deleted when all the browser windows are closed. Cookie __AntiXsrfToken Duration session Description This cookie is used to prevent cross-scripting attacks. It holds a session to verify the login sessions. Cookie MoodleSession Duration session Description This cookie is set by the Moodle. This cookie is used for providing continuity and maintaining the visitor login from page to page. Cookie AWSELBCORS Duration 1 hour Description This cookie is used by Elastic Load Balancing from Amazon Web Services to effectively balance load on the servers. Cookie ols_443 Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie ai_user Duration 1 year Description Microsoft Azure sets this cookie as a unique user identifier cookie, enabling counting of the number of users accessing the application over time. Cookie csrftoken Duration 1 year Description This cookie is associated with Django web development platform for python. Used to help protect the website against Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks Cookie m Duration 2 years Description Stripe sets this cookie for fraud prevention purposes. It identifies the device used to access the website, allowing the website to be formatted accordingly. Cookie cookieyes-* Duration 1 year Description CookieYes sets this cookie for consent solution management. Cookie asid Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description No description available. Cookie YII_CSRF_TOKEN Duration session Description This cookie is used a unique token that used in securing forms and other website inputs against XSS attacks. Cookie 30dc9280-2866-4cf7-bddc-f5362c0308b2 Duration 1 hour Description Description is currently not available. Cookie CONF:30dc9280-2866-4cf7-bddc-f5362c0308b2 Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Description is currently not available. Cookie SignInMessage.9e994fa18756967411b9164be6638491 Duration session Description Description is currently not available. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. Cookie wp-wpml_current_language Duration session Description WordPress multilingual plugin sets this cookie to store the current language/language settings. Cookie __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN Duration 6 months Description Description is currently not available. Cookie Cookies Duration session Description Stores your authenticated session while accessing the Gaiter Dollars portal, maintaining login state, enabling secure redirects, and supporting account features. Cookie UserSettings Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Stores video player preferences like playback quality, captions, speed, volume, and layout to remember personalized viewing settings across Panopto sessions. Cookie idsrv.partial Duration session Description Stores temporary authentication state during multi-step sign-in and logout, enabling session continuity, redirect handling, and access to protected CMS content. Cookie ytidb::LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY Duration Never Expires Description The cookie ytidb::LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY is used by YouTube to store the last search result entry that was clicked by the user. This information is used to improve the user experience by providing more relevant search results in the future. Cookie sp_t Duration 1 year Description The sp_t cookie is set by Spotify to implement audio content from Spotify on the website and also registers information on user interaction related to the audio content. Cookie sp_landing Duration 1 day Description The sp_landing is set by Spotify to implement audio content from Spotify on the website and also registers information on user interaction related to the audio content. Cookie clearoutside_csrf_cookie Duration 2 hours Description Stores a CSRF token to validate requests, preventing unauthorized actions and securing user interactions during form submissions and sessions online. Cookie clearoutside_session Duration 2 hours Description Stores session data to maintain chosen forecast location, display preferences, and recent interactions, ensuring consistent, personalized weather imagery across pages. Cookie 54cd6e38659c1d604586394daae50304f801600aac3abcc7679098638b62d986 Duration session Description Supports Blackbaud webforms by maintaining session state, remembering donor inputs, validating fields, and enabling secure donation processing and form submission. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. Cookie _ga Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to calculate visitor, session and campaign data and track site usage for the site's analytics report. The cookie stores information anonymously and assigns a randomly generated number to recognise unique visitors. Cookie _gid Duration 1 day Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store information on how visitors use a website while also creating an analytics report of the website's performance. Some of the collected data includes the number of visitors, their source, and the pages they visit anonymously. Cookie _gat_gtag_UA_* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store a unique user ID. Cookie _ga_* Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store and count page views. Cookie _gcl_au Duration 3 months Description Google Tag Manager sets the cookie to experiment advertisement efficiency of websites using their services. Cookie vuid Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Vimeo installs this cookie to collect tracking information by setting a unique ID to embed videos on the website. Cookie _hjSessionUser_* Duration 1 year Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjSession_* Duration 1 hour Description Hotjar sets this cookie to ensure data from subsequent visits to the same site is attributed to the same user ID, which persists in the Hotjar User ID, which is unique to that site. Cookie _hjTLDTest Duration session Description To determine the most generic cookie path that has to be used instead of the page hostname, Hotjar sets the _hjTLDTest cookie to store different URL substring alternatives until it fails. Cookie _gat_UA-* Duration 1 minute Description Google Analytics sets this cookie for user behaviour tracking. Cookie _scor_uid Duration 1 year 24 days Description Stores a unique identifier to measure audience size, analyze browsing behavior, and improve advertising relevance and content performance across websites. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyse the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Cookie AWSALB Duration 7 days Description AWSALB is an application load balancer cookie set by Amazon Web Services to map the session to the target. Cookie __utma Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to distinguish users and sessions. The cookie is created when the JavaScript library executes and there are no existing __utma cookies. The cookie is updated every time data is sent to Google Analytics. Cookie __utmc Duration session Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to enable interoperability with urchin.js, an older version of Google Analytics and is used in conjunction with the __utmb cookie to determine new sessions/visits. It is deleted when the user closes the browser. Cookie __utmz Duration 6 months Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to store the traffic source or campaign by which the visitor reached the site. Cookie __utmt Duration 10 minutes Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to inhibit the request rate. Cookie __utmb Duration 1 hour Description Google Analytics sets this cookie to determine new sessions/visits. __utmb cookie is created when the JavaScript library executes and there are no existing __utma cookies. It is updated every time data is sent to Google Analytics. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Cookie IDE Duration 1 year 24 days Description Google DoubleClick IDE cookies store information about how the user uses the website to present them with relevant ads according to the user profile. Cookie test_cookie Duration 15 minutes Description doubleclick.net sets this cookie to determine if the user's browser supports cookies. Cookie elfsight_viewed_recently Duration Less than a minute Description Stores identifiers of recently viewed pages or products to display a personalized recently viewed widget and improve navigation across sessions. Cookie _hashV Duration 1 year 1 month 4 days Description Stores a hashed visitor identifier to preserve portal preferences, attribute marketing campaigns, and optimize campus-visit scheduling, analytics, and user experience. Cookie YSC Duration session Description Youtube sets this cookie to track the views of embedded videos on Youtube pages. Cookie VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to measure bandwidth, determining whether the user gets the new or old player interface. Cookie VISITOR_PRIVACY_METADATA Duration 6 months Description YouTube sets this cookie to store the user's cookie consent state for the current domain. Cookie NID Duration 6 months Description Google sets the cookie for advertising purposes; to limit the number of times the user sees an ad, to unwanted mute ads, and to measure the effectiveness of ads. Cookie __Secure-YEC Duration past Description Description is currently not available. Cookie __Secure-YNID Duration 6 months Description Suivi d'audience et de comportement de lecture du lecteur vidéo YouTube. Uncategorised Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. No cookies to display. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Powered by Job and Internship Board for Students Close Search for: Search Job Board Home Career & Transition Services CATS website Meet the CATS team Employers can submit a job posting Experiential Learning EL website Meet the EL team Bishop’s University Menu Job and Internship Board for Students Service Provided by Career & Transition Services (CATS) and Experiential Learning Keywords Location Full Time Internship Part Time Research Assistant Disclaimer Bishop’s University and Career and Transition Services does not verify or screen the employer and do not endorse or guarantee any job postings or employment opportunities listed on this job board. The data posted on the Board is at the discretion of each employer and Bishop’s University cannot be held responsible for any inconsistencies or errors. The job board is offered as a courtesy service to students and the University is not liable for any damages resulting from its use. It is not the role of the Career and Transition Centre to monitor the recruiting or operational practices of companies, Users are responsible for independently researching and verifying the accuracy and legitimacy of job postings and employers. The University reserves the right to remove, edit, or refuse job postings at its sole discretion. Users should report any concerns or issues with job postings to careerservices@ubishops.ca . Jobs & Internships Currently Available Keywords Location Full Time Internship Part Time Research Assistant RSS Your browser does not support JavaScript, or it is disabled. JavaScript must be enabled in order to view listings. Assistant Technical Director Drama Department On Campus Internship September 1 2026 Student Technician Drama Department On Campus Part Time September 1 2026 Physical Attendant/Préposé(e) à l’accompagnement physique Student Accessibility Services On Campus Part Time August 31 2026 Volunteers needed- Library Book Sale Library Book Sale Lennoxville Part Time August 28 2026 BUSRC Peer Academic Mentor BUSRC On Campus Part Time August 28 2026 Senior Community Development Specialist – Poverty Reduction & Social Inclusion (Part-time contract) Centre for Access to Services in English Hybrid, with regular travel throughout Mauricie and Centre-du-Québec Part Time August 28 2026 Personnel enseignant en Techniques d’éducation spécialisée_TES14 Cegep de Sherbrooke Sherbrooke Part Time August 28 2026 HR Intern – Stagiaire Ressources Humaines Bishop's University Human Resources On campus Internship August 28 2026 Personnel enseignant en Biologie_BIO08 Cegep de Sherbrooke Sherbrooke Part Time August 19 2026 Student Caller for Annual Phonathon Alumni Relations and Philanthropy Office On Campus Part Time August 18 2026 Offre de bourse – Étudiant au doctorat en biologie moléculaire IRDA et Universite de Moncton St-Bruno de Montarville et Moncton Full Time August 6 2026 Chief of finance (CT-FIN-02) Cowansville Institution, Correctional Service of Canada Cowansville Full Time July 9 2026 Horticultural Technician (Plant Production – Controlled Environment Agriculture) Toronto Metropolitan University Toronto Full Time July 6 2026 Master Grower – Controlled Environment Raspberry Production Toronto Metropolitan University Toronto Full Time July 6 2026 Load more listings Got a question? We're here to help! Contact Career & Transition Services: careerservices@ubishops.ca or call us at 819-822-9695. Contact Experiential Learning: EL@ubishops.ca or visit the EL website for more contact details . Career and Transition Services (CATS) website CATS Instagram CATS Facebook Experiential Learning website EL Instagram © 2025 Job Board for Students — All Rights Reserved — Bishop's University Back to Top"
